-- title:
--   Residue order equals U-order at a crossing-presented end
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field with valuation subring $A$, let $F$ be a field extension of $L$ and $\bar F_2$ a field extension of the residue field of $A$, and let $R_2$ be a regular prolongation of $A$ to $F$ with values in $\bar F_2$: a valuation subring `R₂.integers` of $F$ pulling back to $A$ along $L\to F$, together with a surjective ring map $f\mapsto\bar f$ onto $\bar F_2$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with the residue map of $A$, and such that every nonzero $f\in F$ has an $L$-multiple lying in `R₂.integers` with nonzero residue. Let $x_2$ be a place of $\bar F_2$ over the residue field of $A$ (a proper valuation subring containing the image of that field and a principal ideal ring), with $\operatorname{ord}$ the associated normalised order function. Let $\mathcal N_0\subseteq F$ be a Noetherian local subring with $\mathcal N_0\subseteq$ `R₂.integers`, let $C\subseteq L$ be a subring with $C\subseteq A$ whose image in $F$ lies in $\mathcal N_0$, let $\varpi\in C$, and assume every $g\in\mathcal N_0$ is congruent to the image of some $o\in C$ modulo non-units. Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation domain (adically complete for its maximal ideal) with irreducible $\pi$, let $E\ge 1$, let $\sigma\colon W\to\widehat{\mathcal N_0}$ be a ring map into the adic completion of $\mathcal N_0$ at its maximal ideal sending $\pi$ to the image of $\varpi$, and let $\iota\colon\widehat{\mathcal N_0}\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2,W)/(X_0X_1-C(\pi^E))$ be a ring isomorphism carrying $\sigma(o)$ to the constant class `const (π ^ E) o` for all $o\in W$. Let $x,y\in\mathcal N_0$ satisfy $\iota x\equiv\gamma\,$`U (π ^ E)` modulo the ideal generated by `const (π ^ E) π` and `V (π ^ E)`, and $\iota y\equiv\gamma'\,$`V (π ^ E)` modulo the ideal generated by `const (π ^ E) π` and `U (π ^ E)`, for some units $\gamma,\gamma'$, where `U (π ^ E)` and `V (π ^ E)` are the two coordinates of the model. Assume further: for $f\in\mathcal N_0$, $\bar f=0$ if and only if $\iota f$ lies in the ideal generated by `const (π ^ E) π` and `V (π ^ E)`; every non-unit $f$ of $\mathcal N_0$ with $\bar f\ne 0$ has $\operatorname{ord}_{x_2}\bar f>0$; $\bar y=0$; and $\operatorname{ord}_{x_2}\bar x=1$. Then for every $f\in\mathcal N_0$ and every natural number $n$, if $\bar f\ne 0$ then $\operatorname{ord}_{x_2}\bar f\ge 0$, and if moreover $\operatorname{ord}_{x_2}\bar f=n$ then there is a unit $\gamma_f$ of the model with $\iota f-\gamma_f\,$`U (π ^ E)`$^n$ in the ideal generated by `const (π ^ E) π` and `V (π ^ E)`. (Since $n$ is quantified before the implication, the nonnegativity clause is independent of $n$.)
--
--   This is the order law at one end of a node presented by a crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^E)$: on the branch $V=0$ cut out by the kernel of the residue map, the order at the place $x_2$ of the residue of $f$ is exactly the $U$-adic order of $\iota f$ modulo $(\pi,V)$. It is used as the residue-law input when annuli are attached to the ends of such a node, and is cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_layerRationalNodeRing_of_baseRationalNodeRing_layer_chart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_layerRationalNodeRing_of_baseRationalNodeRing_layer_chart) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_layerRationalNodeRing_of_baseRationalNodeRing_layer_chart_of_prime`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_layerRationalNodeRing_of_baseRationalNodeRing_layer_chart_of_prime).
